d. KEAP1 and TP53 co-alteration architecture accepted/closed. SMARCA4 loss effects persist across contexts.\n\nNegative/near-null: research markers D/E/F, broad driver screens (NF1, APC, PIK3CA, BRCA2, SMAD4, ARID1A, RB1), Cas9-low attenuation interactions, ploidy interactions unsupported, CDKN2A-loss negative unresolved near threshold. Signature_c interactions may remain useful but lower priority.\n\nNext most informative analysis: prioritize PTEN conditional robustness: validate H80 if possible; analyze H107 and decide whether PTEN effect persists when SMARCA4 restriction is relaxed. Avoid additional arbitrary PTEN subsets unless H80/H107 produce decisive evidence."
