ll other established predictor-loss contexts. The discovery interval is well above threshold. Because this is the most stringent new clean-context claim and it directly addresses whether MSI-high is independent of the entire supported architecture, I request validation for H133 and keep it active pending that independent result. The MSI-by-driver interactions do not support new modifier claims. H125, MSI-high by TP53-loss interaction, gives signed +0.123 with interval [-0.316,+0.563] and exposed interaction-relevant cells n=24 and 106; H126, MSI-high by KEAP1-loss interaction, gives +0.049 with interval [-0.201,+0.299]. These are underpowered and inconclusive: favorable upper bounds exceed threshold, but lower bounds include zero and estimates are below threshold. I leave both unresolved but closed. H127, MSI-high by SMARCA4-loss interaction, gives signed -0.181 with interval [-0.404,+0.041]; the favorable upper bound is only +0.041, far below the 0.15 threshold, so there is no supported threshold-level evidence in the registered direction. I reject and close H127 rather than post hoc interpreting the negative interval as opposite evidence. The remaining broad screens are negative. H134, media serum 10 versus 2, gives +0.012 with interval [-0.072,+0.095]; the entire favorable side is below threshold, so I reject and close. H135, growth-rate modified SMARCA4-loss interaction, gives signed -0.110 with interval [-0.264,+0.044]; the favorable upper bound is below threshold and the point estimate is opposite the claimed direction, so I reject and close. Overall, these results strengthen the supported supplied-dataset architecture while closing the rare interaction, media-serum, and proliferation-modifier threads. These remain observational associations in this dataset, not causal claims or generalizable biological mechanisms.",
