  "narrative": "No assessment is due at this explore stage. The validated supplied-dataset architecture now has five major components: TP53-loss and KEAP1-loss associated with less-negative composite dependency scores, SMARCA4-loss and MSI-high associated with more-negative scores, and PTEN-loss associated with more-negative scores specifically in TP53-loss-free cells. The most useful next step is to test how far this architecture survives after removing other supported co-alterations, because accepted main effects could still be partly carried by co-occurring TP53-, KEAP1-, SMARCA4-, MSI-, or PTEN-loss contexts. I registered clean-background main effects for TP53-loss, KEAP1-loss, and SMARCA4-loss in cells excluding all other accepted alterations, including MSI-high and PTEN-loss. These mirror the clean MSI-high claim already validated and test whether the major driver-loss associations are independent rather than merely overlapping. The expected directions are the same as the accepted main effects: TP53-loss and KEAP1-loss less-negative, SMARCA4-loss more-negative. If any lower bound falls near or below the 0.15-unit threshold, that would suggest the corresponding accepted main effect is context-dependent or partially co-alteration-driven. I also registered a refined TP53-loss by KEAP1-loss interaction in a cleaner eligibility background excluding SMARCA4-loss, MSI-high, and PTEN-loss. This is the highest-value unresolved thread: the prior interaction estimate is above threshold but its lower bound is only just above zero. A threshold-level clean interaction would support a positive TP53-KEAP1 epistatic pattern; a clean null would justify retaining only the validated main effects and closing the interaction thread. For robustness, I tested the major driver-loss associations within PTEN-loss cells. PTEN-loss is an accepted conditional predictor, so seeing whether TP53-loss, KEAP1-loss, and SMARCA4-loss remain associated in PTEN-loss co-mutant cells clarifies whether the architecture is robust to that co-occurrence. I also tested the accepted PTEN-loss conditional effect in a TP53-loss-free, KEAP1-loss-free, SMARCA4-loss-bearing background, asking whether the PTEN-loss association persists when SMARCA4-loss is present. Finally, I added two specificity/breadth probes using constructed or technical measures. The research_signature_b high-tertile test probes whether the accepted dichotomous TP53-loss by research_signature_b interaction is monotonic or cutoff-sensitive, without assigning biology to the constructed signature. The high screen_roc_auc interaction asks whether better screen quality enhances the observed TP53-loss association; a negative result against this registered direction would simply reject that technical hypothesis and would not support an opposite claim. All proposals are supplied-dataset associations, not causal or generally biological claims.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 10 explore plan. Completed architecture: TP53-loss less negative; KEAP1-loss less negative; SMARCA4-loss more negative; MSI-high more negative; PTEN-loss more negative specifically among TP53-loss-free cells. Major validations already accepted: H80 PTEN-TP53-loss-free and H133 MSI-high clean background. Broad negative screens closed for many canonical/constructed markers, Avana main effect, media serum, sex, proliferation modifier, and most interactions. New registered priorities: (1) clean all-other-alteration-free main effects for TP53, KEAP1, and SMARCA4; these are robustness tests of independence from KEAP1/SMARCA4/MSI/PTEN co-alterations. (2) refined TP53xKEAP1 interaction excluding MSI-high, SMARCA4-loss, and PTEN-loss to resolve the near-threshold unresolved interaction H65/H20; positive threshold-level evidence could justify validation, null could close. (3) TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4 effects among PTEN-loss cells to test robustness to PTEN co-occurrence. (4) PTEN-loss effect in TP53-loss-free, KEAP1-loss-free, SMARCA4-loss cells to test conditional PTEN persistence in SMARCA4-loss context. (5) high-tertile research_signature_b interaction with TP53 in MSI-high-free cells to test cutoff specificity/dose-response of an accepted constructed-signature interaction. (6) high screen_roc_auc interaction with TP53 to test whether screen quality amplifies the driver association. Do not treat constructed signatures/markers as biologically meaningful beyond this dataset. Analyze should prioritize the clean-background driver tests and clean TP53xKEAP1 interaction. Use validation slots mainly if a new threshold-level independent claim emerges, especially the refined TP53xKEAP1 interaction. Interpret all results as associations in the supplied dataset."
