  "narrative": "All newly returned estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction, so positive values support the claimed direction and I compare the lower confidence bound nearest zero against the +0.15 composite-unit threshold. The clean-background main-effect claims are decisive. H137, TP53-loss in a TP53-free eligible background excluding KEAP1-loss, SMARCA4-loss, MSI-high, and PTEN-loss, has signed estimate +0.414 with lower bound +0.315 and n 205 versus 839. H138, KEAP1-loss in the analogous clean background, has signed estimate +0.808 with lower bound +0.775 and n 199 versus 839. H139, SMARCA4-loss in the analogous clean background, has signed estimate +0.798 with lower bound +0.763 and n 209 versus 839. Each lower bound is far above threshold, with valid cell sizes and no zero-inclusive interval, so I accept all three and close them as robustness evidence that the major driver-loss associations are not artifacts carried by the other accepted co-alterations. These are supplied-dataset associations, not causal statements. The PTEN-loss co-mutant contexts also clear threshold: H140 gives TP53-loss among PTEN-loss cells +0.559 with lower +0.274 and n 54 versus 212; H141 gives KEAP1-loss +0.717 with lower +0.519 and n 63 versus 203; H142 gives SMARCA4-loss +0.738 with lower +0.535 and n 58 versus 208. Although exposed cells are smaller, all are valid and intervals remain above threshold. I accept and close these as evidence that the accepted driver-loss associations persist among PTEN-loss co-mutant cells, while noting that small cells increase sensitivity to distributional assumptions. H143 tests PTEN-loss in a TP53-loss-free, KEAP1-loss-free, SMARCA4-loss context and gives signed estimate +0.226 with lower +0.072, upper +0.381 and n 35 versus 228. The interval excludes zero but the lower bound does not exceed threshold, so I keep it unresolved and closed rather than overclaiming threshold-level support; the validated H80 PTEN-loss TP53-loss