  "narrative": "No assessments are due and the independent-validation request budget is exhausted, so the new proposals are discovery-stage refinements rather than validation requests. The already active slow-growth direct comparisons H229-H234 remain important because they complete the prespecified growth-stratum map; if analysis capacity is constrained, they should still be prioritized. The new growth-rate interaction proposals formalize whether the accepted fast-growth stratum associations are merely robust or actually effect-modified. H217-H220 show that the major predictors remain large in fast-growing cells, but direct stratum acceptance does not prove that fast growth modifies their effects. These four interaction tests compare the exposed-minus-comparator raw contrast in fast-growing cells with the complement in the same eligible population. For TP53 loss, where the main raw effect is higher dependency_composite score, I hypothesize positive raw interaction: the TP53-loss effect may be larger in fast-growing cells. For KEAP1 loss, where the main raw effect is also higher score but the fast-growth estimate was slightly smaller than overall, I hypothesize negative raw interaction: rapid proliferation may attenuate the KEAP1-loss association. For SMARCA4 loss and MSI-high, the main raw effects are lower composite scores; therefore, for SMARCA4 I claim positive raw interaction as a test that fast growth attenuates the lower-score association, whereas for MSI-high I claim negative raw interaction as a test that fast growth strengthens the lower-score association. These claims are falsifiable and will be assessed only by the prespecified signed-bound rule. The two research_signature_b interaction proposals address a dataset-structure gap. TP53 loss has strong accepted interactions with constructed signatures A and B, while KEAP1 and the other major predictors are less complete. SMARCA4 loss and MSI-high have not been formally tested against signature B, the signature that was especially strong for TP53. Because research signatures have no assigned biological role, these comparisons are intended to map constructed-assay structure and possible confounding, not to infer biological pathway modification. I register direction -1, corresponding to a stronger lower-score association in the high-signature-B complement group, but expected raw interaction is uncertain. No new validation is requested because zero new requests remain. All interpretations remain dataset-specific observational associations on a composite dependency endpoint, not causal effects or external claims.",
