  "narrative": "I assessed the newly delivered comparisons using the signed 95% Welch intervals and the 0.15 composite dependency-score-unit threshold, without re-orienting the already signed estimates. For the slow-growth stratum, the four core predictor contrasts cleared the accept rule: TP53 loss with higher dependency_composite score (H229, R214: signed +0.375, interval +0.227 to +0.523), KEAP1 loss with higher score (H230, R215: +0.885, +0.796 to +0.974), SMARCA4 loss with lower score (H231, R216: signed +0.918 toward direction -1, lower +0.820), and MSI-high with lower score (H232, R217: signed +0.731 toward direction -1, lower +0.526). These are within-dataset stratum robustness results, not proof of proliferation-rate effect modification. H203 also supports core SMARCA4 loss in KY-library screens (R224: signed +0.830, lower +0.705). The PTEN conditional slow-growth test among TP53-intact cases was suggestive but unresolved (H233, R218: +0.262, lower +0.129, upper +0.395), and CDKN2A slow-growth remained unresolved and low-information (H234, R219: +0.191, lower +0.073). Formal fast-growth interaction tests for TP53, MSI, and the existing KEAP1/SMARCA4 contrasts were all unresolved and centered near small effects, so the data do not establish meaningful growth-rate effect modification; direct fast-stratum acceptance and slow-stratum acceptance together do not imply interaction. The research_signature_b interaction tests were unresolved and should not be interpreted biologically because these signatures are constructed assay features with no assigned pathway or clinical role. I closed the growth-context and signature-interaction investigations because the validation budget is exhausted, the tests are highly multiplicity-burdened, and further subgroup mining in the same observational dataset has low marginal information. Residual concerns include collider/selection sensitivity from conditioning on measured growth rate, missingness in growth-rate and age variables, lack of multiplicity-adjusted intervals, and the endpoint being a composite dependency score rather than a single causal knockout endpoint. No validation was requested because no new requests remain.",
