  "narrative": "No assessments are due and no new independent-validation requests remain. The main conclusions remain unchanged, so this exploration uses remaining discovery capacity on high-information robustness and ambiguity checks rather than new biological mining. First, I register formal interactions between the four major predictors and growth_pattern='adherent'. This tests whether adherence/culture pattern, a potentially important technical phenotype, is associated with effect modification or merely contains the already accepted effects; direct stratum acceptance is not the same as formal interaction evidence. Second, I add formal batch_a interactions for SMARCA4 loss and MSI-high, and reopen the already registered TP53-loss and KEAP1-loss batch_a interaction claims H38/H39 because they remain untested. Complete batch interactions will help determine whether the accepted batch_a estimates reflect general predictor associations or a batch-confounded pattern; these remain observational associations with a composite dependency endpoint. Third, CDKN2A loss is the largest unresolved candidate predictor. I test its effect specifically in TP53-loss cells and test whether the TP53-loss contrast differs from TP53-intact cells, seeking a focused context in which CDKN2A could clear the 0.15-unit threshold. Fourth, PTEN loss is tested in a genetically cleaner background excluding CDKN2A loss, to check whether its secondary context-dependent association is independent of the unresolved CDKN2A modifier. Invalid or small-cell comparisons will remain unresolved and will not be interpreted as null. All claims are dataset-specific and not causal."
