  "narrative": "Applied the prespecified signed-interval rule: accept only when the signed 95 percent lower bound exceeds +0.15 composite units, reject only when the signed 95 percent upper bound is below +0.15, and otherwise leave unresolved. For direction -1 claims, the positive signed estimates already encode support for a negative raw contrast and were not re-signed. All eleven new analyses are valid Welch independent-cell comparisons, but they remain unadjusted and are embedded in a highly multiplicity-burdened exploratory program. The batch_a interaction estimates were imprecise and span the meaningfulness threshold: H38 signed +0.045, interval -0.171 to +0.261; H39 signed +0.133, interval -0.023 to +0.290; H245 signed +0.040, interval -0.107 to +0.187; H246 signed +0.018, interval -0.244 to +0.281. These do not establish scientifically meaningful effect modification by screen_batch batch_a and were closed to avoid false-positive subgroup claims. The adherent growth_pattern interactions also do not clear the threshold: H241 +0.039, -0.188 to +0.266; H242 +0.174, +0.018 to +0.330; H243 +0.070, -0.072 to +0.213; H244 +0.360, +0.110 to +0.610. H242 and H244 are suggestive but remain unresolved because their lower bounds are below +0.15 and because growth_pattern may be correlated with culture, lineage, batch, or other selected technical factors rather than being a clean independent modifier. CDKN2A loss in TP53-loss cells, H247, signed +0.199 with interval -0.053 to +0.452, and the corresponding TP53-loss interaction, H248, signed +0.074 with interval -0.189 to +0.337, are imprecise and do not support CDKN2A as a meaningful predictor or effect modifier within this dataset. This CDKN2A line was closed for this within-dataset investigation. PTEN loss in the clean genetic background excluding TP53, KEAP1, SMARCA4, MSI-high, and CDKN2A abnormalities, H249, signed +0.285 with interval +0.197 to +0.372, clears the threshold and is accepted as a dataset-specific secondary conditional association with lower dependency_composite, meaning stronger composite dependency. This does not make PTEN an unconditional main predictor, does not imply causality, and does not establish external generalizability. No validation request was made because the independent-validation request budget is exhausted.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 19 appraise. The new formal batch_a and adherent growth_pattern interaction tests do not establish effect modification; all remain unresolved. H249 accepted PTEN loss in a clean TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4/MSI/CDKN2A background, signed +0.285 interval +0.197 to +0.372, strengthening the secondary conditional PTEN finding but not converting it into an unconditional primary predictor. CDKN2A remains unresolved and unsupported across focused and broad contexts despite point estimates often near the threshold. Main accepted predictor associations remain unchanged: TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss are associated with higher dependency_composite and weaker composite dependency; SMARCA4 loss and MSI-high are associated with lower dependency_composite and stronger composite dependency. Most other measured predictors, constructed markers, technical variables, and formal interactions are non-supportive or unresolved. Remaining cautions include unadjusted intervals, multiplicity, selection sensitivity from conditional eligibility, collinearity of growth_pattern with culture/batch/lineage-related features, missingness in some covariates, composite endpoint interpretation, and absence of remaining independent-validation budget. The next informative step is external replication and controlled mechanistic perturbation rather than further ad hoc subgroup mining."
}

