  "research_notes": "Final ledger after the last discovery batch. Core accepted validated associations remain unchanged: TP53 loss associated with higher composite score, KEAP1 loss associated with higher composite score, SMARCA4 loss associated with lower composite score, and MSI-high associated with lower composite score. New accepted H309 supports MSI-high lower-score association within TP53-loss cells, with signed estimate +0.884 interval +0.455 to +1.313, but n=24 exposed and no stratum-specific independent validation; treat as dataset-specific. PTEN loss remains secondary and context-dependent: adult PTEN H305 +0.255 interval +0.145 to +0.364 and PIK3CA-mutant PTEN H308 +0.378 interval +0.121 to +0.636 are directionally supportive but unresolved because lower bounds fall below 0.15. Formal PTEN interaction tests H306 and H307 are unresolved. CDKN2A-by-TP53 interaction H310 is unresolved but non-supportive. Technical and constructed-assay interactions H42 H48 H115 remain unresolved, while H43 and H49 are rejected because their signed intervals do not support the claimed positive or negative directions. Validation capacity is exhausted; no further voluntary validation can be requested. Remaining unresolved comparisons are closed for this run. The scientifically defensible final interpretation is that the dataset supports four robust measured predictor directions plus numerous context-specific stratum acceptances, with PTEN as an imprecise secondary association. All conclusions are observational associations on a composite dependency endpoint and do not establish causality or external generalizability."
